    "stdout_len": 0,
    "files": {},
    "stderr_tail": [
     "  Every path in an emitted launch line is shell-quoted (which it must be \u2014 `--gate-off-reason 'PI directive: \u2026'` is why), and quoting SUPPRESSES tilde expansion: `mkdir -p '~/experiments/\u2026'` creates a directory literally named `~`, and the next stage's --init-from then points at a file that does not exist.",
     "  \u26a0\ufe0f The chain will not expand it for you: `~` on the box that GENERATES the command is not `~` on the pod that RUNS it. Paste what `echo $HOME` prints ON THE POD (e.g. /root/experiments)."
    ]
   },
